<title>POLAND: POLISH PLOCK REFINERY BUYS SALT MINE.</title>
<headline>POLISH PLOCK REFINERY BUYS SALT MINE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's state-owned Plock oil refinery on Saturday bought a 51 percent stake in Inowroclawskie Kopalnie Soli SA salt mine from the treasury for 8.5 million zlotys, the privatisation ministry said.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the refinery bought the mine planning to build fuels reserve tanks in its excavation carverns.</p>
<p>It said employees of the mine, based in the central town of Inowroclaw Mazowiecki, would receive 20 percent of shares for half price.</p>
<p>-- Marcin Grajewski +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
